    "type": "Knowledge",
    "text": "Set-builder notation can represent a solution set as an algebraic expression inside braces or as a statement, e.g., S : {x∣x ≤ −1, x ∈ Z} “S is the set of all numbers, x, such that x is less than or equal to −1, and x is an element of the integers.\"",
    "sourcePage": 6,
    "source": "Alberta Draft Mathematics (7–9) Curriculum, June 2026, ©2026 Government of Alberta | Education and Childcare; Draft Curriculum: Optional Classroom Piloting in 2026–27"
